## DO
- Place each part so its bounding box CENTRE and EXTENTS equal the plan row. Compute
  positions from the numbers in the table; do not re-invent the layout.
- Touching parts: surface gap ≤ 0.002 m (flush counts), overlap ≤ 0.002 m (`check_connectivity`
  reports deeper overlap as interpenetration). Every part must be in the ground-touching component
  (a floating part is an ERROR). Add no connector geometry the plan does not list.
- Use `instances` + `symmetry` from the table: mirror pairs at ±x, radial sets around the up axis.
- Build the features each plan description names, at its numbers and counts (the judge's
  checklist verifies them).
- A material per part with the plan's colour.
- Name parts EXACTLY as in the table (PascalCase). One named node/object per part; the
  instances of a part are top-level nodes `Name_0`, `Name_1`, ….

## Detail
{{ detail_advice }}

## DON'T
- No environment sniffing, no `typeof window`, no headless branches — one code path.
- No DOM, canvas textures, image/texture loading, network, file IO, camera/light/render/export calls.
- No helper SDKs or imports beyond the contract's allow-list.
- No placeholders ("TODO", "simplified"); no part off its planned extents by more than the
  contract tolerance (max(1 cm, 10 %) per axis; 3 × that is an ERROR); no unit-cube stand-ins; no
  parts outside the overall bbox.
- Do not change part names, counts or the overall size to "simplify".

